WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.190
In 1992, a civil war in Mozambique ended
with a peace accord signed in Rome.

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.900
The talks were helped along by a Catholic
lay community called Sant'Egidio.

3
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.510
In Northern Ireland, a priest helped open
talks that led to the Good Friday Agreement

4
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.330
in 1998.

5
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.780
War can start in a day.

6
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.490
So how do believers try to
build a peace that lasts?

7
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.410
In this mission, you'll
meet Christian peacemakers,

8
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.630
among them Oscar Romero,
Dorothy Day and Desmond Tutu.

9
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.830
Then you'll see how the United
Nations keeps the peace,

10
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.850
and where it falls short.

11
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:40.590
Your mission: find out how believers
try to build a peace that lasts.
